libmad for amcempega.library: where it came from, and what was changed
=======================================================================

Source: libmad 0.15.1b (Underbit Technologies, Robert Leslie, February
2004), from github.com/markjeee/libmad's import of libmad-0.15.1b.tar.gz.
Its COPYING has the SHA-256 that buildroot records for the release
tarball's (32b1062f7da8...). The decoder's sources, its tables and its
documentation are kept; the build system, minimad, the high-level decoder
API (decoder.c), the generated mad.h and the ARM assembler are left out.

Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING, COPYRIGHT), as all of libmad.
amcempega.library, built from it, is GPL-3.0-or-later.

Changes:

1. (15 November 2026) Debian's security fixes, by Kurt Roeckx (libmad
   0.15.1b-10, as buildroot carries them: package/libmad/0004-md_size.patch
   and 0005-length-check.patch):
   - layer3.c: the size of a Layer III frame's main data checked, and the
     bit reservoir's (md_size: CVE-2017-8372, CVE-2017-8373);
   - bit.c, frame.c, layer12.c, layer3.c: every mad_bit_read checked
     against the end of the buffer first (length-check: CVE-2017-8374).
   Damaged or hostile files can no longer make the decoder read or write
   past its buffers.

2. (15 November 2026) At half the sample rate (MAD_OPTION_HALFSAMPLERATE)
   and at a quarter (MPGA_OPTION_QUARTER, new in stream.h), layer3.c
   leaves out the subbands above what is heard: 16 of the 32 (8 at a
   quarter) get the IMDCT, the rest are zero (III_overlap_z), and the
   alias reduction stops one subband above them. Less work, and nothing
   above the halved rate for the half-rate synthesis to alias. Without
   either option the file decodes as before.

3. (15 November 2026) synth.c: with MPGA_WINDOW_ASM (the 68k's build),
   synth_full's and synth_half's window after the DCT is amcempega.library's
   src/synth_68k.s (mpga_synth calls it a slot at a time): the same sums of
   the same 32-bit products (OPT_SSO), so the same samples; the host builds
   the C as it was.
4. (15 November 2026) synth.h, synth.c: struct mad_synth's mpga_window16
   (0 from mad_synth_init): the window's products 16-bit instead, each
   filter value's 16 fractional bits shifted to 13, each window value's
   low word, one MULS.W each (amcempega.library's medium and low quality);
   in C on the host (mpga_window16), in assembler on the 68k, the same.
